# Copy to .env.local.

# ─── GitHub sign-in (REQUIRED) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The console has no anonymous mode: every user signs in through GitHub OAuth,
# and every GitHub call (reading repos, committing the workflow, setting repo
# secrets) is performed with that user's own token. There is no server-side
# GitHub token anywhere.
#
# Create the app at  https://github.com/settings/developers  → "New OAuth App"
#   Homepage URL:               http://localhost:3000
#   Authorization callback URL: http://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback/github
#
# The requested scope is `read:user user:email repo workflow`. `repo` lets the
# console read private repositories; `workflow` is required on top of it to
# commit `.github/workflows/quality-gate.yml`. If you upgraded from an older
# build, sign out and back in once to grant `workflow`.
#
# These are the Auth.js v5 names. The older next-auth v4 names
# (GITHUB_ID / GITHUB_SECRET / NEXTAUTH_SECRET) are still read as a fallback.
AUTH_GITHUB_ID=
AUTH_GITHUB_SECRET=
# Only needed if Auth.js can't infer the deployment URL itself (it usually can,
# `trustHost` is on). Set it to the site's public origin when it can't.
AUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000
# Any long random string: `openssl rand -base64 32`
AUTH_SECRET=

# ─── Gemini / Sonar (OPTIONAL fallback) ──────────────────────────────────────
# The gate needs a GEMINI_API_KEY Actions secret on each installed repo. The
# install wizard lets the user paste one per repo; if they leave it blank, the
# console falls back to the value below and writes THAT as the repo secret.
# SONAR_TOKEN works the same way (SonarCloud is skipped when neither is set).
GEMINI_API_KEY=
SONAR_TOKEN=
# NOTE: there is deliberately no SONAR_ORGANIZATION fallback. The SonarCloud org
# is per-repo (`sonar-project.properties` → `sonar.projectKey=<org>_<repo>`) and
# a console-wide default silently points repos at the wrong org. Enter the org
# in the install wizard instead — the console commits the file only then.

# ─── Quality Gate action ref (OPTIONAL) ──────────────────────────────────────
# The generated workflow runs the gate with
# `uses: NonnaritRammaneekultawat-6609650459/test-github-marketplace@<ref>`.
# Defaults to the `1.1` release tag (the action repo's tags are unprefixed —
# `1.1`, `1.0`, not `v1.x`) so one bad commit on the action's `main` can't break
# every install at once. Set `main`, another tag, or a commit SHA to change it;
# "Save changes" on an installed repo re-commits the workflow.
AQG_ACTION_REF=1.1
